---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
const crumbs = [{ label: 'Advertising disclosure', href: '/advertising-disclosure/' }];
---
<Page title="Advertising Disclosure" description="How Sign of Nine is funded: display advertising served by a network, and affiliate links to books where they appear, always marked." h1="Advertising disclosure" lead="Sign of Nine is free to read and funded by advertising. This page says how, and what that does and does not affect." crumbs={crumbs} eyebrow="Legal" updated="2026-10-17">
  <section aria-labelledby="ads">
    <h2 id="ads">Display advertising</h2>
    <p>The site shows advertisements served by Google AdSense and, later, by other advertising networks. Advertisers do not see what you type into the calculators, and no page is written or ordered to suit an advertiser. The advertising networks use cookies and similar technologies, which you can accept or refuse through the consent message shown to visitors in the UK and the European Economic Area; the <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> explains the detail.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="affiliate">
    <h2 id="affiliate">Affiliate links</h2>
    <p>Some pages may link to books about numerology through affiliate programs. If you buy through such a link, the site may earn a small commission at no extra cost to you. Affiliate links are marked where they appear. The site does not sell sponsored posts, paid links or product placements.</p>
  </section>
  <section aria-labelledby="independence">
    <h2 id="independence">Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>What a page says about a number is decided by the method on the <a href="/editorial-approach/">editorial approach</a> page and by the sources it cites, never by advertising. Questions about this policy go to the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Page>
